  {
   "id": "L10",
   "law": "the nullity is seam-dependent: level-junctions vs support-element junctions",
   "status": "SURVIVES (as a fence)",
   "evidence": "level seam gives delta = (L_j-|S_j|)^+ (0 on every support-rich state); the dual element seam gives delta' = (|S_j|-L_j)^+, which at the official ratio |S_j| = 256 L_j equals 255 L_j, i.e. delta'_total = 255 t = 255*2^33 -- the two canonical latent expansions of the SAME junction differ by q^(255t). Gate 0 (PP2.0) must fix the expansion before 'E[q^delta] <= 2^21' has a meaning"
  },
  {
